  "notes": "{穏|おだ}やか is a na-adjective meaning calm, peaceful, gentle, or mild.\n\nFORMS:\n- {穏|おだ}やかな + noun (attributive)\n- {穏|おだ}やかに + verb (adverbial)\n- {穏|おだ}やかだ (predicative)\n- {穏|おだ}やかで (te-form)\n\nCOMMON USES:\n- {穏|おだ}やかな{天気|てんき}: calm weather\n- {穏|おだ}やかな{海|うみ}: calm sea\n- {穏|おだ}やかな{性格|せいかく}: gentle personality\n- {穏|おだ}やかな{顔|かお}: a serene face\n- {穏|おだ}やかに{話|はな}す: to speak gently\n- {穏|おだ}やかに{暮|く}らす: to live peacefully\n- {気持|きも}ちが{穏|おだ}やかになる: to feel calm\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {静|しず}か: quiet, silent (emphasizes lack of noise)\n- {温和|おんわ}: gentle, mild (often for personality/climate)\n- {平穏|へいおん}: peaceful, tranquil (more formal)\n- おとなしい: docile, quiet (often for personality)\n\nNUANCE:\n{穏|おだ}やか suggests a pleasant, undisturbed state—whether weather, mood, personality, or atmosphere.",
